{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/25131-why-auspices-have-no-additionnal-ban","id":25131,"title":"Why auspices have no additionnal ban ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-07T08:41:52-08:00","id":25131,"title":"Why auspices have no additionnal ban ?","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> Be member of a tribe adds a law/ban/rule in the oath of the moon, but the auspices do not.<br /> It may be interesting to deal with another rule when you are Irraka or Elodoth or whatever.<br /> <br /> So, this is my proposition:<br /> for Irraka, it could be \u00abnever show your true aim\u00bb<br /> Rahu: \u00abWin or die trying\u00bb<br /> Elodoth: \u00abPain for guilty\u00bb<br /> Cahalith: \u00abLet no one howl louder than you\u00bb or \u00abhowl in first\u00bb<br /> Ithaeur: \u00abUnderstand them\u00bb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:30:01-08:00","id":25586,"title":"","content":"Those really put a dent in individuality. The Oath of the Moon is designed to be personally interpreted by those who swear it. Tribal oaths included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:59:09-08:00","id":25635,"title":"","content":"You also don't have a choice about your Auspice. An Irraka is an Irraka. That was chosen for them. They never got a chance to accept that ban as something that meshes with their view on what their purpose is.<br /> <br /> The Tribal bans are something you agree to. The Harmony sins are something inherent to the nature of balancing spirit and flesh. What does this Auspice ban come from? Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T05:27:30-08:00","id":26437,"title":"","content":"You get Auspice from Lunes, Lunes are spirits, and the key of any binding with spirits is a ban.<br /> I like this idea what every kind of werewolf groups which are patronized by spirits have to respect a ban.<br /> Metagaming speaking, it is quick way to describe each Auspice.<br /> The Auspice ban should be really generic. It would have to be interpreted. It is given by the werewolf's Ancestor: Luna through her phases.<br /> <br /> It is wrong to say they don't have the choice concerning Auspice, they can refuse their Auspice, and They can become Pure instead. (It will require to perform a rite)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T06:52:27-08:00","id":26472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObiWanKennedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea what every kind of werewolf groups which are patronized by spirits have to respect a ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what your totem is for. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObiWanKennedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is wrong to say they don't have the choice concerning Auspice, they can refuse their Auspice, and They can become Pure instead. (It will require to perform a rite)</div> </div> </div> </div>The key difference between the patronage of Luna and the Anshega totems, is that Luna remains distant, less her touch drive her children insane. The spirits the Pure serve virtually enslave their packs.<br /> <br /> And those bans you designed there don't even serve to account for the different Aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T09:35:15-08:00","id":26554,"title":"","content":"I think Werewolves have enough problems that they don't need an additional weakness piled on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:14:08-08:00","id":26612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObiWanKennedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/25131-why-auspices-have-no-additionnal-ban?p=26437#post26437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get Auspice from Lunes, Lunes are spirits, and the key of any binding with spirits is a ban.<br /> I like this idea what every kind of werewolf groups which are patronized by spirits have to respect a ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a fair representation of how getting an Auspice is presented in the games. You aren't a Rahu because you have the lunes as your patrons. You are a Rahu because your spirit-side was awakened during Luna's full moon phase. You don't strike a deal with the lunes to get your Auspice. You don't &quot;bind&quot; with them. They're simply the conduit for Luna's selection (as Ephsy mentioned, Luna keeps her distance).<br /> <br /> As for choice, yes you can strip yourself of an Auspice. But you don't get to say, &quot;Hey Luna, I think I should be an Irraka not a Elodoth.&quot; You can reject the phase you were chosen under for no Auspice; you still don't get to pick which one you started with.<br /> <br /> I also think Ephsy and Rani are dead on with both Auspice Bans been too restrictive given the variety of ways to express an Auspice, and that the Forsaken already have enough problems. I'm open minded to the concept of Auspices not being 100% bonuses, but I'm not convinced Bans are the way to go about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:44:48-08:00","id":26708,"title":"","content":"Auspice is more like an inborn talent/drive/perspective than any kind of deal or binding. Bans on Auspice would be like saying that because you're Irish, you <i>have </i>to be an alcoholic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}